WEBVTT

00:08.902 --> 00:14.662
Let's laugh and cry.
chanto waraimasho, nakimasho

00:15.162 --> 00:20.752
We need to fill up our hearts.
kokoro no nakami wo juujitsu sasenakuccha
Subs originally by Froth-Bite
Manually retyped by #Retrofit@IRC.Rizon.Net
Raws by Darkside-Raws

00:20.792 --> 00:29.342
Making matching memories with you...
anata to osoroi no omoide tsukuruno ga

00:29.342 --> 00:31.212
...is important.
daiji daiji

00:32.592 --> 00:35.142
Sometimes I become...
sunao ni narenakattari

00:35.472 --> 00:38.972
...almost dishonest and mean
ijiwaru shichaisouna hi aruno

00:40.472 --> 00:41.812
That's because...
sore wa...

00:43.812 --> 00:46.562
I love you and adore you,
daisuki de taisetsu de

00:46.692 --> 00:49.902
and I don't want to be apart from you.
hanaretaku nai sei nano nante

00:51.862 --> 00:52.862
That's the truth.
henne

00:55.412 --> 01:02.122
I just want to cuddle...
hontou wa itsumo nuku nuku shitetai

01:02.452 --> 01:04.462
...with you.
futaride

01:05.462 --> 01:11.172
So let's laugh and cry.
dakara waraimashou, nakimashou

01:11.842 --> 01:17.262
We need to keep our hearts warm.
kokoro no ondo wo atatame awanakucha

01:17.472 --> 01:25.772
The fate that made us meet...
anata to deaeta unmei ho subetega

01:25.772 --> 01:27.602
...is important.
daiji daiji

01:43.392 --> 01:44.522
Now...

01:50.652 --> 01:51.902
Yes?

01:51.902 --> 01:52.782
What is it?

01:54.822 --> 01:56.572
Kozue-chan!

01:56.572 --> 01:59.122
I bought some taiyaki at Akando.

01:59.532 --> 02:02.162
Would you like to have some with everyone?

02:02.832 --> 02:04.122
Sounds good.

02:04.122 --> 02:05.672
I heard that, Kozue-chan.

02:06.172 --> 02:09.212
I reserve the one with the most sweet bean paste.

02:09.212 --> 02:11.462
Shiratori-kun, I'll let you have the second best one.

02:12.052 --> 02:13.302
Yes, yes.

02:13.302 --> 02:15.552
Now that the deal's done, let's eat!

02:18.722 --> 02:19.722
"Crack"?

02:28.732 --> 02:31.022
It's been acting up recently.

02:31.022 --> 02:33.242
It would squeak.

02:33.242 --> 02:35.202
I thought I was careful, but...

02:35.782 --> 02:37.412
I'm sorry, Kozue-chan.

02:37.412 --> 02:38.202
It's okay.

02:38.202 --> 02:40.912
It's an old building to begin with.

02:40.912 --> 02:44.002
I'm sorry to inconvenience you.

02:45.002 --> 02:47.252
Is this the toolbox?

02:47.542 --> 02:49.002
Yes, it is.

02:49.002 --> 02:51.042
I'm sorry to involve you too.

02:51.042 --> 02:52.422
It's not a problem.

02:52.422 --> 02:53.632
You found it?

02:53.632 --> 02:54.302
Yes.

02:55.052 --> 03:00.262
Anyway, this storage room is almost like an antique store.

03:00.262 --> 03:01.262
I know.

03:01.262 --> 03:03.272
There's a lot in here.

03:03.272 --> 03:04.022
Yes.

03:04.022 --> 03:06.852
We've been storing things here for years.

03:06.852 --> 03:07.892
For example...

03:09.522 --> 03:12.152
This is 50 year-old umeboshi.

03:12.152 --> 03:14.902
The condition is just perfect.

03:15.322 --> 03:18.992
The peerless taste that fills your mouth is just wonderful!

03:18.992 --> 03:20.622
Kozue-chan...

03:20.912 --> 03:23.912
Oh, I'm so sorry!

03:23.912 --> 03:24.832
Oh?

03:25.582 --> 03:27.212
What's the matter, Kozue-chan?

03:27.212 --> 03:29.082
There's something behind it...

03:31.042 --> 03:32.132
A diary?

03:32.277 --> 03:34.404
Aoba Soichiro

03:34.922 --> 03:36.672
Aoba Soichiro!

03:36.672 --> 03:37.922
What is it?

03:37.922 --> 03:40.302
This is Great Grandfather's diary.

03:40.302 --> 03:43.432
Great Grandfather? You mean yours?

03:43.432 --> 03:44.222
Yes.

03:44.222 --> 03:47.602
He was the landlord of this place before I was born.

03:52.732 --> 03:53.862
Is this...

03:53.862 --> 03:56.152
A map of Narutakisou?

03:56.152 --> 03:56.992
It is.

03:56.992 --> 04:00.412
Could it be a treasure map?

04:00.412 --> 04:01.872
No way.

04:01.872 --> 04:05.122
"I found an old page in the storage room today."

04:05.122 --> 04:09.162
"In it, I found..."

04:09.922 --> 04:13.082
"...a map that indicates the location of a treasure."

04:15.592 --> 04:20.432
"I truly wish that a descendant of mine would find this treasure."

04:21.822 --> 04:23.182
Treasure of Narutakisou

04:23.182 --> 04:24.512
A treasure?!
Treasure of Narutakisou

04:24.512 --> 04:28.372
Treasure of Narutakisou

04:29.062 --> 04:30.312
Narutakisou's...

04:30.892 --> 04:32.062
Treasure?!

04:32.062 --> 04:33.232
Yes!

04:33.232 --> 04:34.482
This is it!

04:34.482 --> 04:36.362
Isn't this a great discovery!?

04:36.362 --> 04:38.822
It is an old building.

04:39.242 --> 04:42.282
There should be a treasure or two.

04:43.872 --> 04:45.912
Don't you think so?

04:45.912 --> 04:48.332
I don't think...

04:48.332 --> 04:49.332
Very possible!

04:51.582 --> 04:54.832
The ancient treasure was hidden so close to us...

04:55.792 --> 04:58.462
The hidden treasure is ours now!

04:58.462 --> 05:03.762
The numerous notes written on the map must be the clues to find the treasure.

05:03.762 --> 05:06.262
How much would the treasure be?

05:06.262 --> 05:07.972
A week's worth of wages?

05:07.972 --> 05:09.772
Or could it be two weeks worth?!

05:09.772 --> 05:12.312
I can't even imagine it!

05:12.312 --> 05:14.482
Calm down, Asami.

05:15.192 --> 05:17.022
Um, everyone...

05:17.022 --> 05:18.192
Okay!

05:18.572 --> 05:21.952
We're commencing the hunt for the treasure...

05:21.952 --> 05:24.952
...buried under Narutakisou!

05:24.952 --> 05:26.022
Yeah!

05:26.702 --> 05:27.122
Where should we start?

05:27.122 --> 05:27.742
They unite their souls...
Where should we start?

05:27.742 --> 05:30.292
They unite their souls...
Let's start out by decrypting this writing.

05:30.292 --> 05:31.042
They unite their souls...
What language is this?

05:31.042 --> 05:32.082
What language is this?
...only when there's something like this.

05:32.082 --> 05:32.782
...only when there's something like this.
No clue...

05:32.782 --> 05:33.002
...only when there's something like this.

05:33.002 --> 05:33.712
Hey there Shiratori-san,
...only when there's something like this.

05:33.712 --> 05:35.212
Hey there Shiratori-san,

05:35.832 --> 05:38.252
I hope you aren't thinking...

05:38.252 --> 05:43.802
...that Kozue-chan's great grandfather wrote down a bunch of lies?

05:44.842 --> 05:46.852
No, I'm not...

05:48.852 --> 05:50.142
Kozue-chan...

05:52.432 --> 05:54.562
I wonder what the treasure is.

05:54.562 --> 05:56.812
I can't wait, right, Shiratori-san?

05:56.812 --> 05:58.022
Yeah...

05:58.022 --> 05:59.192
I know!

05:59.402 --> 06:01.402
Start the search!

06:01.402 --> 06:02.692
Roger!

06:04.492 --> 06:07.122
Roger...

06:12.082 --> 06:14.332
Where's my spot?

06:14.962 --> 06:16.712
Let's see...

06:16.712 --> 06:20.922
"The one who visits Narutakisou shall see the 3rd pillar from the East."

06:20.922 --> 06:22.212
3rd pillar...

06:22.592 --> 06:24.132
Ignoring me?!

06:24.132 --> 06:26.592
One, two, three...

06:26.592 --> 06:27.552
This is it!

06:28.092 --> 06:30.262
So, what's next?

06:30.262 --> 06:31.682
Hang on.

06:31.682 --> 06:32.932
What's this?

06:33.272 --> 06:35.522
There are so many scratches.

06:35.522 --> 06:39.112
Is it a code indicating the location of the treasure?

06:40.732 --> 06:41.652
Momo-san!

06:42.282 --> 06:43.232
Well...

06:43.232 --> 06:46.822
"These are the marks made by a girl...

06:46.822 --> 06:49.282
...until she was 12 years old..."

06:49.282 --> 06:50.492
Mark of...?

06:50.492 --> 06:52.872
"Of her height."

06:54.042 --> 06:55.542
Her height?

06:55.542 --> 06:59.252
A girl must have marked her growth on it once upon a time.

06:59.252 --> 07:00.592
Twelve...

07:02.922 --> 07:04.882
I'm twelve too...

07:04.882 --> 07:06.842
Fight, Asami.

07:06.842 --> 07:09.392
Mom, is it the sardines?

07:09.392 --> 07:11.852
Am I not eating enough?

07:11.852 --> 07:12.852
Let's see the next one!

07:13.812 --> 07:16.732
"The large tree standing in the center of the courtyard..."

07:16.732 --> 07:20.862
"It is the lord of Narutakisou exceeding 300 years of age!"

07:20.862 --> 07:22.652
This is it.

07:22.652 --> 07:25.692
Wow, this tree is 300 years old!

07:25.692 --> 07:28.362
"Stand by its roots, and...

07:28.362 --> 07:29.282
All right!

07:29.282 --> 07:32.032
That's where the treasure is, right?!

07:32.032 --> 07:33.582
...and look up."

07:33.582 --> 07:34.492
Huh? Up?

07:40.212 --> 07:41.382
Let's see...

07:41.382 --> 07:47.302
"I hope you can enjoy the greatness of the one who senses the change...

07:47.302 --> 07:49.262
...of seasons all year long."

07:50.432 --> 07:52.682
"Enjoy"...?

07:56.142 --> 07:58.692
OH, NO!

08:03.272 --> 08:05.152
How is it, Mom?

08:05.482 --> 08:06.982
Did you find anything?

08:07.612 --> 08:10.322
"There is something hidden under the porch."

08:10.322 --> 08:12.532
"It's a secret treasure nobody knows about."

08:12.532 --> 08:14.452
It better be real this time!

08:14.452 --> 08:16.702
I can't tell either!

08:16.702 --> 08:19.872
This map has too many worn out and torn spots.

08:19.872 --> 08:21.212
Let's see...

08:21.212 --> 08:26.672
"It is not known who dug it,

08:27.052 --> 08:29.132
but there is a mysterious old well."

08:29.422 --> 08:30.592
"It is..."

08:30.592 --> 08:31.932
It is?

08:32.892 --> 08:36.852
What are you doing, Mom?

08:36.852 --> 08:38.392
"It is the reason...

08:38.682 --> 08:44.192
...why it is so cool under the porch even in the middle of the summer."

08:44.192 --> 08:46.522
"A perfect spot for cooling off."

08:48.402 --> 08:50.242
It's so cool.

08:51.322 --> 08:52.782
Damn it!

08:52.782 --> 08:55.122
So much with the hints for locating the treasure!

08:55.122 --> 08:57.292
They're all irrelevant!

08:57.792 --> 08:59.452
Don't give me that!

08:59.452 --> 09:01.962
There are too many places on this map I can't read!

09:01.962 --> 09:07.632
But I see that Narutakisou hasn't changed at all for a long, long time.

09:08.592 --> 09:10.382
I know.

09:10.382 --> 09:11.802
That's it!

09:12.052 --> 09:15.682
That means the treasure is still in its original place!

09:15.682 --> 09:16.552
I see.

09:16.972 --> 09:19.392
So as long as we can read the map...

09:19.392 --> 09:20.562
Um...

09:20.562 --> 09:22.562
What is it, Lieutenant Shiratori?

09:22.562 --> 09:23.772
That.

09:24.022 --> 09:25.812
Is it okay to leave it like that?

09:25.812 --> 09:27.982
Oh, yeah, that's right.

09:29.192 --> 09:32.402
I'll count on you to do the rest, Lieutenant.

09:32.402 --> 09:34.862
I won't waste the sacrifice of your own life!

09:34.862 --> 09:36.662
Hey! Momono-san!

09:36.662 --> 09:37.242
Adieu!
Hey! Momono-san!

09:37.242 --> 09:38.202
Adieu!

09:40.202 --> 09:41.622
Let's see...

09:41.622 --> 09:43.922
Will you be okay, Shiratori-san?

09:44.422 --> 09:45.712
Yeah.

09:45.712 --> 09:47.632
I should be able to handle it by myself.

09:49.052 --> 09:50.052
Oh?

09:50.052 --> 09:51.172
What's the matter?

09:51.712 --> 09:53.512
There are no nails.

09:56.642 --> 09:58.552
Damn, I don't get it!

09:58.552 --> 10:00.222
This isn't good.

10:00.222 --> 10:02.982
The treasure is so close, yet...

10:02.982 --> 10:06.152
Then let's just start digging everywhere.

10:06.152 --> 10:10.522
We just need to be able to read it, right?

10:10.522 --> 10:12.822
Do you have an idea?

10:13.742 --> 10:15.992
I guess I do...

10:17.372 --> 10:19.372
Where are you going?

10:20.452 --> 10:22.792
We need to buy some nails.

10:22.792 --> 10:24.252
I will go...

10:24.252 --> 10:25.832
...along with him too.

10:25.832 --> 10:26.792
Tamami-chan?

10:27.122 --> 10:29.002
Hey! What about the treasure?

10:29.252 --> 10:32.842
I need to buy some things too.

10:32.842 --> 10:34.632
Is that okay, Shiratori-san?

10:34.632 --> 10:35.092
Of course.
Is that okay, Shiratori-san?

10:35.092 --> 10:36.012
Of course.

10:36.012 --> 10:37.092
Geez!

10:37.092 --> 10:40.012
We'll dig up the treasure before you come home!

10:41.642 --> 10:43.852
It turned into a big deal.

10:43.852 --> 10:46.392
Everyone loves these events.

10:46.392 --> 10:48.352
They're always bored.

10:48.352 --> 10:50.232
Oh, Tamami-chan.

10:50.942 --> 10:54.862
It's all thanks to Kozue-chan's great grandfather's diary.

10:55.402 --> 10:58.952
What kind of person was your great grandfather?

10:58.952 --> 11:00.412
Well...

11:01.082 --> 11:06.542
I remember that he was a very kind person.

11:07.332 --> 11:10.422
Whenever I visited him, he let me sit on his lap...

11:11.212 --> 11:13.252
...and told me fun stories.

11:13.962 --> 11:16.472
He sounds very nice.

11:16.472 --> 11:17.932
I loved him.

11:18.882 --> 11:22.682
He passed away when I was very young.

11:34.612 --> 11:35.482
But...

11:36.742 --> 11:41.662
I wonder what the treasure he wrote about is.

11:42.622 --> 11:44.662
I am a bit curious.

11:49.502 --> 11:52.502
Treasure of Narutakisou, huh?

12:04.342 --> 12:05.802
Thank you!

12:06.682 --> 12:09.182
This should be enough.

12:09.182 --> 12:10.852
I'm done over here too.

12:11.482 --> 12:12.732
Tamami-chan.

12:13.932 --> 12:15.022
What did you buy?

12:15.022 --> 12:17.482
Futaba Electric

12:17.482 --> 12:20.232
It's a surprise for later.
Futaba Electric

12:20.232 --> 12:21.402
Futaba Electric
Oh, yeah?

12:21.862 --> 12:23.862
Then shall we head back?

12:23.862 --> 12:26.032
Can we go somewhere else too?

12:27.282 --> 12:29.912
I would like to make another stop.

12:33.372 --> 12:34.542
A watermelon?

12:34.542 --> 12:37.542
I'm sure everyone is exhausted from treasure hunting.

12:37.542 --> 12:38.882
Here ya go! Thank you!

12:39.712 --> 12:42.002
I picked the best of the crop.

12:42.002 --> 12:43.592
Thank you, sir.

12:44.262 --> 12:45.382
I'll carry it.

12:45.382 --> 12:46.012
Yeah.

12:46.882 --> 12:49.262
It's tough being a landlady, huh?

12:49.262 --> 12:52.262
Getting snacks ready for the residents, fixing the house...

12:52.642 --> 12:54.312
You're doing great.

12:54.312 --> 12:56.102
Oh, I'm not that...

12:56.102 --> 12:57.272
You're great!

12:57.272 --> 12:58.692
Tamami-chan...

12:58.692 --> 13:01.982
Anyway, Narutakisou sure has survived well.

13:02.362 --> 13:06.742
I heard that they were planning to raze it once upon a time.

13:07.402 --> 13:08.242
Raze?

13:08.242 --> 13:09.322
Narutakisou?

13:09.742 --> 13:11.662
Oh? You don't know?

13:11.662 --> 13:12.912
Well, no wonder.

13:13.622 --> 13:18.082
It's something I heard from my grandpa when I was a kid.

13:20.252 --> 13:24.742
It happened when my grandpa was young, right after the war.

13:24.742 --> 13:24.762
The whole of Tokyo was a burnt field.
It happened when my grandpa was young, right after the war.

13:24.762 --> 13:26.572
The whole of Tokyo was a burnt field.

13:26.572 --> 13:27.092
Narutakisou

13:27.092 --> 13:28.532
But in the middle of that, Narutakisou miraculously survived,
Narutakisou

13:28.532 --> 13:31.802
But in the middle of that, Narutakisou miraculously survived,

13:31.802 --> 13:34.812
and became the resting place for those who lost their homes.

13:34.812 --> 13:36.272
Over here!

13:38.062 --> 13:40.852
But when the restoration started...

13:42.732 --> 13:47.742
Narutakisou became a nuisance to the officials...

13:48.242 --> 13:51.662
...who were developing the city.

13:52.492 --> 13:56.702
"Let's raze this old place, and build a new high-rise."

13:57.662 --> 13:59.212
"So move out!"

14:00.042 --> 14:01.882
"That's ridiculous!"

14:02.752 --> 14:06.132
The man who told them so was the landlord back then.

14:06.132 --> 14:10.842
The other residents united together, and created a big commotion.

14:20.102 --> 14:22.732
So, after a few similar incidents,

14:22.732 --> 14:26.402
Narutakisou still remains as it was, in the middle of other high-rises.

14:26.822 --> 14:28.492
Grandpa told me,

14:28.492 --> 14:31.912
"That really made our day."

14:31.912 --> 14:35.872
"Really, Soichiro-san was a great landlord."

14:36.582 --> 14:39.202
So he was a great man.

14:39.202 --> 14:42.462
I'd expect nothing less from your great grandfather.

14:45.212 --> 14:47.132
Then let's hurry home.

14:48.132 --> 14:53.262
We need to find the treasure that your great grandfather protected.

14:54.012 --> 14:54.892
Yes.

14:57.142 --> 14:57.892
Not here!

14:58.022 --> 14:58.602
Not here!!

14:58.682 --> 14:59.732
Not here!!!

14:59.812 --> 15:01.062
Not here!!!!

15:01.392 --> 15:03.902
There is no treasure anywhere!

15:04.272 --> 15:06.652
I'm completely exhausted.

15:07.772 --> 15:09.362
I'm sleepy...

15:09.362 --> 15:11.032
Don't fall asleep, Mom.

15:14.032 --> 15:15.702
I guess you've hit a wall.

15:15.702 --> 15:17.492
Oh, welcome home.

15:17.492 --> 15:21.162
It's because that map is too old.

15:21.582 --> 15:24.632
I can't make out all the critical spots.

15:27.342 --> 15:29.342
I expected this.

15:40.932 --> 15:42.522
It's clear now.

15:42.522 --> 15:44.142
That's pretty.

15:44.142 --> 15:45.352
That's right.

15:46.102 --> 15:51.112
This is the infrared scope-mounted digital camera, deScale No. 1!

15:51.692 --> 15:55.412
Any fading letters or signs will be made clear with this.

15:55.412 --> 15:58.742
Tamami-chan, that's awesome.

15:58.742 --> 16:02.372
Why would a neighborhood electronics shop carry such a thing?

16:02.372 --> 16:04.922
What was the meaning of all of our effort?

16:04.922 --> 16:06.882
Hey, this is...

16:07.292 --> 16:08.592
Did you find something?

16:08.592 --> 16:09.542
Yes.

16:09.542 --> 16:10.382
Um...

16:11.592 --> 16:14.842
"The truth hidden on this map...

16:14.842 --> 16:19.472
...shall be revealed only to those who are well-folded."

16:21.472 --> 16:25.392
What does "well-folded" mean?

16:26.812 --> 16:28.062
Mom?

16:28.062 --> 16:29.192
I don't know...

16:29.522 --> 16:34.362
It probably means very well-mannered.

16:34.362 --> 16:37.202
The well-mannered among us...

16:37.612 --> 16:38.822
They would be...

16:40.242 --> 16:41.372
Certainly...

16:42.872 --> 16:44.872
So.

16:45.412 --> 16:46.622
Me?

16:46.622 --> 16:48.132
Me too?

16:48.382 --> 16:49.882
We have no choice.

16:49.882 --> 16:52.672
It says "well-mannered."

16:52.672 --> 16:54.262
Good luck, you two.

16:54.262 --> 16:55.632
Give it your best!

16:55.632 --> 16:57.682
But still...

16:57.682 --> 16:58.842
Yeah...

17:06.102 --> 17:08.402
I don't see anything...

17:08.652 --> 17:10.312
Well-folded...

17:10.612 --> 17:12.402
Easier said...

17:13.442 --> 17:16.192
So? Do you see anything?

17:16.192 --> 17:18.612
Hang on a minute.

17:19.412 --> 17:20.622
It folded over.

17:23.832 --> 17:24.702
Folding!

17:25.292 --> 17:26.122
Huh?

17:26.122 --> 17:28.212
Well-folded!

17:28.502 --> 17:31.502
So, if we fold it along these creases...

17:31.502 --> 17:33.802
Shiratori-san, that's inside out.

17:33.802 --> 17:34.842
Oh, I see.

17:34.842 --> 17:36.842
If we fold the map properly, then...

17:36.842 --> 17:37.472
Then?

17:41.932 --> 17:43.182
This is the spot!

17:44.602 --> 17:46.432
Hurry, Onii-chan!

17:46.432 --> 17:48.442
Shiratori-kun, don't damage it.

17:48.442 --> 17:50.192
I know.

17:54.572 --> 17:55.282
The treasure!

17:55.282 --> 17:56.362
Money!

17:56.652 --> 17:58.952
It really exists!

17:58.952 --> 18:00.112
Treasure...

18:00.702 --> 18:02.872
I didn't expect it here...

18:02.872 --> 18:05.372
No wonder it felt so good to sit on this spot.

18:05.372 --> 18:07.792
Good job, Kozue-chan.

18:09.252 --> 18:10.582
Kozue-chan,

18:11.882 --> 18:12.502
I'm opening it.

18:13.632 --> 18:14.422
Yes.

18:24.512 --> 18:26.602
This is the treasure?

18:28.892 --> 18:30.062
Um...

18:30.062 --> 18:33.862
"To those who have cleared all obstacles and found this,

18:33.862 --> 18:34.772
congratulations."

18:35.192 --> 18:39.782
"Any problem can be overcome if you put your efforts together."

18:39.782 --> 18:43.822
"That is Narutakisou's Treasure. Good job."

18:43.822 --> 18:44.742
Um...

18:45.282 --> 18:46.792
What is that supposed to mean?

18:46.792 --> 18:50.122
Didn't your great grandfather's diary say...

18:50.122 --> 18:52.502
Yes, it did.

18:54.582 --> 18:57.882
"We found a map that indicates the location of the treasure."

18:57.882 --> 18:59.302
"I hope..."

18:59.302 --> 19:00.302
Oh?

19:00.722 --> 19:02.882
The pages are stuck together.

19:02.882 --> 19:04.722
Oh, they are.

19:06.512 --> 19:09.062
"We can't let go of the treasure,

19:09.062 --> 19:12.272
so all the residents searched throughout the property."

19:12.272 --> 19:16.652
"They always unite their efforts for anything like this."

19:16.652 --> 19:20.692
"We looked all through the day and night, and finally found the treasure."

19:20.692 --> 19:23.912
"But all there was in it was a piece of paper that said 'Good job.'"

19:23.912 --> 19:27.952
"Looks like it was a prank left behind by our ancestors."

19:27.952 --> 19:29.412
"Oh, dear."

19:29.412 --> 19:33.252
"It ticked us off, so we put the treasure chest back in its place."

19:33.792 --> 19:38.422
"I truly wish that a descendant of mine would find this treasure."

19:39.422 --> 19:43.512
Your great grandfather and his people located this treasure...

19:43.512 --> 19:47.012
And we were tricked just like them...

19:47.352 --> 19:49.062
They got us.

19:49.062 --> 19:51.022
Sounds like he was a humorous man.

19:51.562 --> 19:53.642
I mean your great grandfather.

19:54.392 --> 19:56.152
It's a photo?

19:56.152 --> 19:57.862
That's Narutakisou.

19:57.862 --> 20:00.482
At Narutakisou, 1946?

20:00.482 --> 20:05.202
So, is this your great grandfather's photo?

20:05.202 --> 20:06.572
It looks like it.

20:07.782 --> 20:09.582
The old Narutakisou, huh?

20:09.582 --> 20:13.082
They're also residents tricked by this prank.

20:13.082 --> 20:14.582
And this picture is the proof.

20:14.582 --> 20:15.082
Let me see!
And this picture is the proof.

20:15.082 --> 20:16.122
Let me see!
They really got us.

20:16.582 --> 20:20.132
People who live here are always bored.

20:20.752 --> 20:23.632
Doesn't he look like Onii-chan?

20:24.842 --> 20:26.432
Who?

20:26.432 --> 20:27.342
Him.

20:27.722 --> 20:29.932
Yeah, he does!

20:30.602 --> 20:32.932
And doesn't the next person like like Kozue-chan?

20:32.932 --> 20:34.812
Me?

20:34.812 --> 20:37.812
Hey, they look good together.

20:37.812 --> 20:39.562
They must be dating.

20:39.862 --> 20:43.282
She's like Momo-san, looking so poor.

20:43.282 --> 20:44.072
What?!
She's like Momo-san, looking so poor.

20:44.072 --> 20:44.742
What?!

20:44.742 --> 20:45.992
There's Johnny too!

20:45.992 --> 20:46.862
How cute!

20:46.862 --> 20:48.452
Stop it. How embarrassing.

20:49.072 --> 20:50.162
Work pants...

20:50.162 --> 20:53.332
You would look like this girl, if you acted more elegant.

20:53.332 --> 20:54.952
What?!

20:55.542 --> 20:58.002
The treasure of Narutakisou, huh?

21:02.752 --> 21:06.422
Hey, let's take a picture of us too!

21:06.422 --> 21:08.472
And we'll hide it in this chest.

21:09.052 --> 21:12.932
We'll make the later residents go through the same pain decades from now.

21:15.982 --> 21:17.812
I second it!

21:17.812 --> 21:20.562
But we'd better fix the door before that.

21:20.562 --> 21:21.692
That's right.

21:21.692 --> 21:24.532
Well, I guess it's for our beloved Narutakisou.

21:24.532 --> 21:26.192
Then everyone help!

21:26.192 --> 21:27.952
Momo-san, you're so selfish.

21:27.952 --> 21:29.612
Well, I guess.

21:29.612 --> 21:32.162
Can you help us with our work too?

21:32.162 --> 21:33.912
Jeez, Mom.

21:36.702 --> 21:37.582
Is it done yet?

21:37.582 --> 21:38.122
Hurry!
Is it done yet?

21:38.122 --> 21:39.172
Hurry!

21:39.172 --> 21:41.002
Ready?

21:43.132 --> 21:44.962
Hey, Tamami-chan!

21:59.402 --> 22:05.912
One day, I drew a picture all over a canvas,
itsu no hika canvas ni e ippai

22:05.992 --> 22:11.712
a picture of 7-colored dreams.
nanairo no yume egaita

22:13.132 --> 22:19.592
When I noticed, I was a bit more grown up.
ki ga tsukeba sukoshi otona ni natte

22:19.842 --> 22:24.892
What have I found?
nani wo mitsuketandarou

22:26.852 --> 22:33.602
In this aimless daily life,
yuka ate no nai mainichi no nakade

22:33.852 --> 22:39.532
I found something that's most important.
ichiban taisetsuna koto ni kizuita

22:40.532 --> 22:46.372
Yes, it's always all right,
donna tokidemo sousa daijoubu

22:46.372 --> 22:48.622
because you are here.
kimi ga irukara

22:48.832 --> 22:55.002
Holding these unforgettable thoughts,
wasurenai kono omoi dakishimete

22:55.502 --> 23:01.342
I will start walking the path of the halted fantasy again,
mouichido togireta yume no fantasy

23:01.342 --> 23:05.972
at my own speed.
aruitemiyou boku no speed de

23:21.942 --> 23:22.192
The Next Episode Preview Corner

23:22.192 --> 23:25.232
Everyone's photo came out nicely.
The Next Episode Preview Corner

23:25.232 --> 23:26.272
